  "how_to_tell_apart": "Czech shows itself with jsem/jsi rather than Slovak som/si, co rather than čo, když rather than keď, jen rather than len, tady/teď/tohle rather than tu/teraz/toto, and the letters ě, ř and ů, which standard Slovak does not use. Shared short items such as to, je, na, už and ne are not decisive. Polish (already in the reference lists) also shares some Slavic function words but not ě/ř/ů or the forms above.",
